1
00:00:01,793 --> 00:00:06,840
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:30,947
Lily, you all right back there?

3
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:32,949
I'm fine, Dad. [chuckles]

4
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,743
This place looks great!

5
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:41,875
But, Dad, it's a bit hot.

6
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:45,712
What do you mean? It's so windy!

7
00:00:45,795 --> 00:00:49,174
All right, let me turn up the AC.

8
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:51,301
-Hon! We don't have one!
-[laughing]

9
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:52,469
We don't?

10
00:00:52,552 --> 00:00:53,887
-Nope!
-Come on, Dad!

11
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:58,099
It's been broken since forever!

12
00:00:58,183 --> 00:01:01,978
That's because we've never
had the money for it.

13
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,563
Don't worry.

14
00:01:03,646 --> 00:01:06,066
Once we settle down in Poblacion Ardiente,

15
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:07,442
we'll have enough money to spare.

16
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:12,363
And it won't be long until
I build my own private law firm.

17
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:14,491
-Wow!
-Me too, hon.

18
00:01:14,574 --> 00:01:17,911
I'll put up a weekend day care center.

19
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:19,496
-Whoa!
-Good idea, Mom.

20
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:23,583
And… it won't be long
until we get a new car too.

21
00:01:23,666 --> 00:01:24,667
What do you think?

22
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:25,960
[Camia and Lily] Ta-da!

23
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:27,670
[laughing]

24
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:29,631
[Dante] Look, we're almost there!

25
00:01:29,714 --> 00:01:31,466
[rattling sound]

26
00:01:31,549 --> 00:01:32,967
-Oh.
-Oh.

27
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:34,344
-[Lily] Dad.
-[Camia] Hey.

28
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,096
-[chuckles]
-Hon, what happened?

29
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,264
-[Dante] Hold on.
-[Lily chuckles]

30
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:39,808
[engine cranking]

31
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:41,768
-Oh, no, Dad.
-It won't start.

32
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:43,269
Let me try again.

33
00:01:43,353 --> 00:01:44,771
[engine cranking]

34
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:46,731
-Oh. It still won't start.
-Still won't, huh.

35
00:01:46,815 --> 00:01:48,066
Take a deep breath, everyone.

36
00:01:48,149 --> 00:01:49,400
[all inhale deeply]

37
00:01:50,068 --> 00:01:51,694
-[engine starts]
-There you go!

38
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:53,029
Ta-da!

39
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:55,365
-Ta-da!
-See that? It won't fail us.

40
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:57,700
-[Lily] You should take it easy, Mom.
-[Dante] You get worried so easily.

41
00:01:57,784 --> 00:01:59,202
[Lily] All right. We're almost there.

42
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:00,870
We're almost there!

43
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:02,205
-Look!
-That's the arch, right, Dad?

44
00:02:02,288 --> 00:02:05,208
-[Camia] Is there a celebration?
-[Lily] Yeah.

45
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:06,543
[Dante] Oh.

46
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:08,920
-[engine sputtering]
-Hey.

47
00:02:11,256 --> 00:02:13,633
-[Lily] Dad.
-What is it this time?

48
00:02:13,716 --> 00:02:15,426
-I'm sure it's nothing serious.
-[Camia] What?

49
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:18,680
[engine cranking]

50
00:02:18,763 --> 00:02:20,682
I don't think it wants us
to go through, hon.

51
00:02:20,765 --> 00:02:23,643
Don't worry. Just hold on.

52
00:02:23,726 --> 00:02:24,769
Take another deep breath.

53
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:25,812
[Dante and Lily inhale deeply]

54
00:02:25,895 --> 00:02:28,648
[engine cranking]

55
00:02:28,731 --> 00:02:29,732
Oh, boy.

56
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:31,109
-Hon!
-It still won't start.

57
00:02:31,192 --> 00:02:35,363
Uh… Why don't you take over?
You know the drill, right?

58
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:36,948
I can do it with my eyes closed.

59
00:02:37,031 --> 00:02:38,366
[Lily chuckles]

60
00:02:38,449 --> 00:02:39,742
[feel-good music playing]

61
00:02:39,826 --> 00:02:40,994
[Lily] Go, Dad!

62
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:42,162
THANK YOU FOR COMING
ARDIENTE TOWN

63
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,997
Are you ready, Mom?

64
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,456
Release the handbrake!

65
00:02:46,624 --> 00:02:47,917
Dad, do you need help?

66
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:49,627
All right, come here!

67
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:50,587
Game.

68
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:52,714
[together] One, two, three!

69
00:02:52,797 --> 00:02:55,425
[both grunting]

70
00:02:55,508 --> 00:02:57,302
-Just keep pushing!
-[Dante] Okay!

71
00:02:58,928 --> 00:03:01,639
[Dante grunting]

72
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:02,599
Push!

73
00:03:03,349 --> 00:03:05,435
I'm on it! Come on, Lily! Push!

74
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:07,020
-[Lily straining] Yes, Dad.
-[Dante] Harder!

75
00:03:07,103 --> 00:03:08,104
A bit more!

76
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:12,317
-[engine starts]
-There we go! [shouts with joy]

77
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:15,361
-[Dante whooping]
-Let's go, Dad!

78
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:19,741
-Oh, no.
-Oh.

79
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:21,826
[Dante] Hon, what happened?

80
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,536
I'm not sure.

81
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,747
Uh… Pop open the hood.

82
00:03:25,830 --> 00:03:28,791
Dad, it must be the spark plug again.

83
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:30,460
-[siren wailing]
-Lily, what do you know

84
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:31,794
about spark plugs?

85
00:03:31,878 --> 00:03:34,797
But wasn't that the problem last time?

86
00:03:34,881 --> 00:03:36,132
[Dante] Oh, right.

87
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:39,802
Lily…

88
00:03:50,855 --> 00:03:51,731
What's the problem here?

89
00:03:52,565 --> 00:03:54,943
Nothing, sir. Our car just broke down.

90
00:03:55,818 --> 00:03:56,861
[bodyguard 1] Name, please.

91
00:03:58,154 --> 00:03:59,364
Atty. Dante Cruz.

92
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:01,991
This is my daughter, Lily,
and my wife, Camia.

93
00:04:02,075 --> 00:04:03,201
We're from Manila.

94
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:06,329
I was assigned here in Poblacion Ardiente.

95
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:08,456
What happened?

96
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:10,333
[bodyguard 2] Their car broke down,
Governor.

97
00:04:10,416 --> 00:04:11,960
Then have it towed.

98
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:16,256
Copy that. Please tell him we're on it.

99
00:04:17,590 --> 00:04:21,261
[quiet music playing]

100
00:04:31,396 --> 00:04:32,480
[Dante] Sir…

101
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:34,732
What's going on?

102
00:04:34,816 --> 00:04:35,775
Governor's orders.

103
00:04:35,858 --> 00:04:37,068
Who?

104
00:04:37,151 --> 00:04:39,570
Governor Julio Ardiente.

105
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:42,073
He's in that car.
We'll take you to the car shop.

106
00:04:42,782 --> 00:04:45,034
[tense music playing]

107
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:50,373
[bodyguard 1] Sir, just get in your car.
Governor will handle it.

108
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:54,127
-Let's go.
-[tense music intensifies]

109
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:56,587
[crowd cheering, applauding]

110
00:05:00,466 --> 00:05:03,511
[drums playing]

111
00:05:03,594 --> 00:05:05,054
THANK YOU VERY MUCH!

112
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:07,598
[emcee] My fellow townspeople!

113
00:05:07,682 --> 00:05:11,769
The beloved father of Poblacion
Ardiente has arrived!

114
00:05:11,853 --> 00:05:13,271
Let's all welcome Governor Julio,

115
00:05:13,354 --> 00:05:16,941
and the whole Ardiente family!

116
00:05:17,025 --> 00:05:19,027
[crowd cheering, applauding]

117
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:22,613
[brass band playing cheerful music]

118
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:27,410
[man chanting] Governor Julio!
Governor Julio!

119
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:31,247
Governor Julio! Governor Julio!

120
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:34,917
Governor Julio! Governor Julio!

121
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:37,420
-Governor Julio!
-[women screaming]

122
00:05:54,937 --> 00:05:56,397
Governor!

123
00:05:57,106 --> 00:05:58,524
Madam.

124
00:05:58,608 --> 00:06:00,443
[screaming]

125
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:06,324
THANK YOU VERY MUCH!

126
00:06:06,407 --> 00:06:09,994
[brass band playing cheerful music]

127
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:11,412
[man] Governor Julio!

128
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:14,999
[crowd cheering, applauding]

129
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:33,768
A very happy and prosperous
festival to all of us!

130
00:06:33,851 --> 00:06:36,062
[crowd cheering, applauding]

131
00:06:37,146 --> 00:06:40,108
[Julio chuckles]

132
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:46,364
For 80 years, the Ardiente
family has been serving you,

133
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:49,325
our beloved citizens.

134
00:06:49,408 --> 00:06:54,205
From my ancestors to my parents,

135
00:06:54,288 --> 00:06:57,917
and up to my administration today,

136
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:01,003
alongside my daughter, Emilia.

137
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:03,047
[crowd cheering, applauding]

138
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:09,804
[Julio] Since then,

139
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:14,058
the Ardiente family
has been there for you.

140
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:17,186
We are your family too.

141
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:19,647
[crowd cheering, applauding]

142
00:07:19,730 --> 00:07:21,482
[Julio] And that will never change.

143
00:07:22,066 --> 00:07:25,611
We will continue to provide

144
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:28,865
for the needs of everyone here
in Ardiente.

145
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:32,368
[crowd cheering, applauding]

146
00:07:34,787 --> 00:07:36,330
[emcee] Governor Julio,

147
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:42,503
the people of Ardiente
have a surprise for you!

148
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:49,343
[brass band playing]

149
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:55,183
[crowd cheering, applauding]

150
00:08:01,981 --> 00:08:07,236
[crowd chanting] Governor Julio!
Governor Julio! Governor Julio!

151
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:12,325
Governor Julio! Governor Julio!
Governor Julio!

152
00:08:12,408 --> 00:08:16,162
Governor Julio! Governor Julio!

153
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:23,252
[band stops playing]

154
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:24,879
My fellowmen…

155
00:08:25,588 --> 00:08:27,840
We're supposed to celebrate.

156
00:08:28,716 --> 00:08:31,302
But you're making me emotional.

157
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:36,015
[crowd, adoringly] Aww.

158
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:39,227
[Julio] I honestly wasn't expecting

159
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,812
that you prepared a gift

160
00:08:41,896 --> 00:08:46,275
to recognize your humble servant.

161
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:48,069
But I have two concerns.

162
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:51,906
First, that makes me feel old.

163
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:55,576
[laughing]

164
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,537
Second…

165
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,122
[laughing]

166
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:05,836
You only erect a statue for dead people.

167
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:08,714
Do you want your Governor Julio
to die early?

168
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:11,926
[crowd] No!

169
00:09:12,009 --> 00:09:15,471
-Sir, how's the car?
-Hi, sir. It's all fixed.

170
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:19,016
Really? Thank you so much!
How much do I owe?

171
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,561
No need, sir.

172
00:09:21,644 --> 00:09:22,687
What do you mean?

173
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:25,189
The governor already paid for it.

174
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:26,899
But still… Come on. Take this.

175
00:09:26,983 --> 00:09:31,946
Oh, no. If you insist,
I won't help you next time.

176
00:09:32,029 --> 00:09:33,155
[Julio] In all seriousness…

177
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:34,240
[chuckles] Oh, boy.

178
00:09:34,323 --> 00:09:37,326
I'd like to express
my gratitude for your gift.

179
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:40,621
And I want you to keep this in mind…

180
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:48,546
As long as this statue
stands firm in our town…

181
00:09:50,047 --> 00:09:55,219
you will continue to have
honest service and leadership

182
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:59,181
as promised
by your very own Governor Julio!

183
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:02,393
[crowd cheering, applauding]

184
00:10:02,476 --> 00:10:05,271
[crowd chanting] Governor Julio!
Governor Julio!

185
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:06,564
Viva Ardiente!

186
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:08,482
[crowd] Viva Ardiente!

187
00:10:08,566 --> 00:10:10,151
Viva Ardiente!

188
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:12,862
[crowd] Viva Ardiente!

189
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:15,406
Viva Ardiente!

190
00:10:15,489 --> 00:10:18,159
[crowd] Viva Ardiente!

191
00:10:18,242 --> 00:10:20,453
[crowd cheering, applauding]

192
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:27,209
[Julio] Thank you.
And now, let's welcome your BFF,

193
00:10:27,293 --> 00:10:29,920
everyone's best friend,

194
00:10:30,004 --> 00:10:35,426
Mayor Emilia Ardiente-Torillo!

195
00:10:35,509 --> 00:10:38,471
[crowd cheering, applauding]

196
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:47,271
My friends!

197
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:49,482
Hi!

198
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:52,360
[crowd] Hi, friend!

199
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:55,029
One more time, okay?
Let's put our hands together

200
00:10:55,112 --> 00:10:59,075
for the father of Poblacion Ardiente,

201
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:03,371
the greatest father
in the world, Governor Julio!

202
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:05,498
[crowd cheering, applauding]

203
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:08,167
I love you, Dad.

204
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:09,251
[mouthing] I love you.

205
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:13,756
[crowd chanting] Governor Julio!
Governor Julio! Governor Julio!

206
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:18,386
Governor Julio! Governor Julio!

207
00:11:18,469 --> 00:11:22,765
Governor Julio! Governor Julio!

208
00:11:24,558 --> 00:11:27,645
[soft music playing]

209
00:11:36,654 --> 00:11:39,281
Yes, this is going to be our new home!

210
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,741
-[grunts]
-[giggles]

211
00:11:41,325 --> 00:11:43,244
[Lily] The front yard is huge!

212
00:11:43,327 --> 00:11:46,205
But why don't we have neighbors?

213
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:48,207
Um…

214
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,792
It's more peaceful this way, sweetie.

215
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:52,753
No one will think of doing us harm here.

216
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:55,673
-[goat bleating in distance]
-Is this all ours?

217
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:58,134
It will be in two years,
once I pay it all off!

218
00:11:58,217 --> 00:11:59,176
Look over there!

219
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:02,012
That's where
we'll put up our day care center.

220
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:03,180
[chuckles]

221
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:06,308
We'll have the peaceful life
you've been dreaming of.

222
00:12:12,606 --> 00:12:14,650
[soft music playing]

223
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:21,907
The people here are so nice. Right, Mom?

224
00:12:21,991 --> 00:12:25,536
They had a lot of giveaways.
It was like a birthday party.

225
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:28,164
That man also helped us,

226
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:29,790
and the shop fixed our car for free!

227
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:32,918
Lily, free things don't make good people.

228
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:35,421
It's not right to judge people, hon.

229
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:38,716
That's true.
But you shouldn't trust people too easily.

230
00:12:38,799 --> 00:12:41,802
The governor acted surprised
when he saw the statue.

231
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:43,220
How is that possible

232
00:12:43,304 --> 00:12:45,389
when the funding for it
came from his office?

233
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:49,101
Of course, that adds
to the drama, his charisma,

234
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:50,603
and appeal to the masses!

235
00:12:50,686 --> 00:12:51,937
Did you see how the townspeople acted?

236
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:55,566
They're like fanatics
when they shout his name.

237
00:12:55,649 --> 00:12:58,277
But, Dad, don't you trust the governor?

238
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:03,199
Lily, of all the wealthy people
and politicians I met in Manila,

239
00:13:03,282 --> 00:13:05,826
I can count with one hand
those who are truly good.

240
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:08,120
Maybe you're right, Dad.

241
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:11,040
The death threats you received
came from rich people.

242
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:14,376
[gloomy music playing]

243
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,962
[sighs] Come on, Dad.

244
00:13:17,046 --> 00:13:19,298
I hear you and Mom talking about them.

245
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:22,384
And I'm not scared
as long as I'm with you.

246
00:13:24,428 --> 00:13:27,681
But, Dad, maybe the Ardientes
are different.

247
00:13:27,765 --> 00:13:33,771
They seem like nice rich people.
The whole town loves them.

248
00:13:35,731 --> 00:13:37,858
[sighs] Lily…

249
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:39,527
If you're a good person,

250
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:42,488
you won't need armed bodyguards
to protect you.

251
00:13:42,571 --> 00:13:44,782
But maybe, they need bodyguards

252
00:13:44,865 --> 00:13:49,119
because they always stand by what's right.
They get into disagreements.

253
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,621
But if you're a truly good person,

254
00:13:50,704 --> 00:13:53,165
you won't be afraid to die
for what you're fighting for.

255
00:13:53,249 --> 00:13:57,878
But if you love your family,
you will choose your battles.

256
00:13:57,962 --> 00:14:00,631
You'll think about whether
your beliefs are worth dying for.

257
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:03,175
So, it all goes back to me.

258
00:14:03,259 --> 00:14:06,053
That's why we're here, right?
To start a new life.

259
00:14:06,136 --> 00:14:08,597
Dante, I'm just reminding you…

260
00:14:09,431 --> 00:14:11,308
-in case…
-[clicks tongue]

261
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:15,479
You think too much. Can you relax a bit?

262
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:18,065
Don't you know that your husband
has nine lives?

263
00:14:18,148 --> 00:14:19,525
-Nine…
-Right, Lily?

264
00:14:20,526 --> 00:14:22,194
-[Lily and Dante meowing]
-You two are ganging up

265
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:25,281
on me again. That's enough.
I still have to empty those boxes.

266
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:26,657
-[Dante] No, just stay here.
-[Camia] Hon…

267
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:28,325
Hey, I'm fixing up stuff too.

268
00:14:29,493 --> 00:14:31,829
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

269
00:14:31,912 --> 00:14:36,208
[Lily] <i>I'd always hear the words</i>

270
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:40,796
<i>"fight," "hope," and "change"</i>
<i>when my parents would talk.</i>

271
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:47,761
<i>And how change could only</i>
<i>be achieved through love.</i>

272
00:14:47,845 --> 00:14:51,056
<i>Love for oneself, love for others,</i>

273
00:14:52,057 --> 00:14:53,809
<i>and love for our nation.</i>

274
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:03,527
Look at them. They're enjoying the food.

275
00:15:03,611 --> 00:15:07,239
You know, I love
it when I see the poor people happy.

276
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:11,619
That's why the poor also love
the Ardientes.

277
00:15:12,286 --> 00:15:13,287
[man] They always support you.

278
00:15:13,370 --> 00:15:16,665
What time are we going home?
It's so hot here!

279
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:19,418
Can't we go home later? It's fun here.

280
00:15:20,252 --> 00:15:22,421
[playful music playing]

281
00:15:22,504 --> 00:15:23,589
You're the only one enjoying.

282
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:25,966
Because whenever there's food,
you're happy.

283
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:27,051
Can you stop eating?!

284
00:15:27,134 --> 00:15:28,761
-[plate clatters]
-[Loring] Hey!

285
00:15:28,844 --> 00:15:32,097
Your brother's not done eating, Arnaldo.

286
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:34,058
-Don't waste the food.
-Hey.

287
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:36,435
Are you two fighting again?

288
00:15:36,518 --> 00:15:38,103
He started it, Mom.

289
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:39,980
I didn't do anything, but he--

290
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,273
Where's your father?

291
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:44,652
[tense music playing]

292
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:47,655
[woman laughing] You're funny, sir.

293
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:52,534
By the way, if you need help

294
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:56,163
from the municipality,

295
00:15:56,246 --> 00:15:57,998
you can come to me.

296
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,500
-Especially with your…
-Really, sir?

297
00:15:59,583 --> 00:16:01,377
Of course! Especially with your costumes.

298
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:04,254
-[woman] Really?
-We'll get you girls even better ones.

299
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:06,131
-[woman giggling]
-[Raul] What's your name again?

300
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:07,508
We are the Choco Babes.

301
00:16:07,591 --> 00:16:09,885
-Oh, Choco Babes.
-Yes.

302
00:16:12,304 --> 00:16:13,889
Hi, friends!

303
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:15,140
[together] Hi, Auntie!

304
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:18,602
-[snickers]
-[dark playful music playing]

305
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:22,731
[Julio] Thank you very much.

306
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:24,566
[Loring] I'll get another plate.

307
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:26,360
[Arnaldo] Grandpa, Diego's
gobbling the food up.

308
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:28,696
-[Loring] I'll get you a new plate.
-Look at him.

309
00:16:29,613 --> 00:16:31,907
Diego! That's enough eating.

310
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:42,209
Um, Diego too much food
isn't good for your health.

311
00:16:42,292 --> 00:16:45,254
You know how much I worry about you.

312
00:16:47,214 --> 00:16:50,175
-I'll get you… some take-out later.
-[Julio] Hey.

313
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:51,844
It'll be our secret.

314
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:53,846
[Arnaldo] Where did you get
your suit made?

315
00:16:55,431 --> 00:16:57,307
-[man] How old are you?
-Twelve, sir.

316
00:16:57,391 --> 00:17:00,644
You should start being
a politician in your school.

317
00:17:00,728 --> 00:17:01,812
[Julio] At the student council.

318
00:17:01,895 --> 00:17:06,025
That's like politics,
but on a smaller scale.

319
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:08,485
[playful music playing]

320
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:10,404
Look at him, Grandpa.

321
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:12,448
[Julio] I see him.

322
00:17:15,784 --> 00:17:16,827
Swallow it.

323
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:20,706
Swallow it!

324
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:30,090
[Dante] "You know
whom I represent, don't you?" he asked.

325
00:17:30,174 --> 00:17:34,053
"My cashier tells me you're
the head clerk of Thomson and French."

326
00:17:34,928 --> 00:17:35,971
"That's correct."

327
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:37,765
She's asleep.

328
00:17:38,515 --> 00:17:39,391
I know.

329
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:44,438
-That book again?
-You know it's her favorite.

330
00:17:44,521 --> 00:17:45,773
It isn't for kids.

331
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:49,568
Our daughter is smarter than other kids.

332
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:00,829
-[exclaims]
-[Loring] Oh!

333
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:02,331
Oh, sorry, ma'am!

334
00:18:02,414 --> 00:18:04,792
Can you be more alert?

335
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:06,418
Is that so difficult to do?

336
00:18:06,502 --> 00:18:08,087
I'm sorry.

337
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:09,588
[Raul] Dad, congratulations.

338
00:18:09,671 --> 00:18:11,548
That was a very successful event.

339
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:14,176
-What you said was brilliant.
-[Julio] Emilia…

340
00:18:14,259 --> 00:18:17,221
-Yes, Dad?
-I hope you got some pointers.

341
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:22,184
Always remind the people
that they're important to you.

342
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:24,853
They've got tiny brains.

343
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:28,440
Praise them a little,
and they'll worship you.

344
00:18:28,524 --> 00:18:32,361
And in return, even if you do
something wrong later on,

345
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:36,323
they will fight for you and defend you.

346
00:18:36,406 --> 00:18:38,283
Do you understand what I'm saying?

347
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:41,161
Yes, Papa.

348
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:42,663
I hope so.

349
00:18:43,747 --> 00:18:45,332
-Good night.
-We're not in public anymore.

350
00:18:45,415 --> 00:18:47,584
There's no need for that.

351
00:18:48,585 --> 00:18:51,505
Good night, Grandpa. We're going to bed.

352
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:53,549
Good night, Arnaldo.

353
00:18:53,632 --> 00:18:54,716
[Diego] Good night, Grandpa.

354
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:57,469
I'm not done with you yet.

355
00:18:59,596 --> 00:19:01,849
Wipe the sauce from your mouth.

356
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:07,104
Good night, Mom.

357
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:09,022
-Good night.
-[kisses]

358
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:12,276
Go to bed now.

359
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:19,074
[gloomy music playing]

360
00:19:22,619 --> 00:19:23,495
Thank you.

361
00:19:25,622 --> 00:19:28,250
-You're not done with that?
-Not yet.

362
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:31,795
<i>365 Days of Love and Guidance.</i>

363
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:34,423
Lily will read this every morning.

364
00:19:34,506 --> 00:19:35,799
[scoffs]

365
00:19:35,883 --> 00:19:39,178
Don't you mean 365 days
of flattering each other?

366
00:19:40,429 --> 00:19:41,763
-Fine, I'll stop.
-[chuckles]

367
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:44,933
Just kidding. I think it's a great idea.

368
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:47,311
Me too.

369
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:53,734
I hope this is the last time
we move houses.

370
00:19:54,776 --> 00:19:56,236
I hope…

371
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,906
this town will serve as our paradise.

372
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:02,409
Hon, anywhere is paradise…

373
00:20:02,492 --> 00:20:04,578
as long as I'm with you and Lily.

374
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:15,964
-What's wrong?
-Let's talk.

375
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:18,634
Do we really have to?

376
00:20:18,717 --> 00:20:20,802
We've been together
the whole day, remember?

377
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:22,804
Have you no sense of decency?!

378
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:23,972
What were you doing at the plaza?

379
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:25,515
What did I do wrong this time?

380
00:20:26,099 --> 00:20:28,727
I was just being friendly to the girls.

381
00:20:29,394 --> 00:20:31,355
We should support the youth
because they're the future, right?

382
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:34,483
-How dare you!
-What did I do?

383
00:20:34,566 --> 00:20:37,236
You hit on anything that wears a skirt!

384
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:38,904
They were wearing shorts, not skirts.

385
00:20:38,987 --> 00:20:40,197
You pervert!

386
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,823
-[glass shatters]
-Hold on!

387
00:20:41,907 --> 00:20:43,242
-[suspenseful music]
-[Raul] I think I know why

388
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:44,868
you're acting like that.

389
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:46,370
Is it because they called you "Auntie"?

390
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:48,038
-See?
-[glass shatters]

391
00:20:48,121 --> 00:20:50,791
[Raul] You're out of your mind.
What's so wrong with that?

392
00:20:50,874 --> 00:20:52,292
Did you want them to call
you "sis" instead?

393
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:53,585
Sleep it off. You're just tired.

394
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:55,170
-You jerk!
-Let's not--

395
00:20:58,423 --> 00:21:01,009
You really won't stop?
What do you want? Huh?

396
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:01,927
[Raul] Tell me!

397
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:08,767
[Julio] What's going on here?

398
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:09,977
Nothing, Papa.

399
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:13,855
You're fighting again, aren't you?

400
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:16,108
No, we were just having a discussion.

401
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:18,568
Hey.

402
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:22,698
What do you take me for? I'm not an idiot!

403
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:27,327
Come. Let's talk outside. Go.

404
00:21:28,745 --> 00:21:29,663
Out!

405
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:33,625
[dark dramatic music playing]

406
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:37,462
[Julio] Let's talk here.

407
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:42,092
This…

408
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:49,057
This is all your fault.

409
00:21:49,641 --> 00:21:51,893
If a married couple is having problems,

410
00:21:51,977 --> 00:21:55,689
it's always the wife's fault.

411
00:21:55,772 --> 00:21:58,066
-You…
-[whimpers]

412
00:21:59,276 --> 00:22:00,360
You…

413
00:22:00,902 --> 00:22:04,072
and your weaknesses as a woman!

414
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:07,784
Straighten yourself out! Understood?!

415
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:13,749
[sobbing]

416
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:26,511
[sniffles]

417
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:28,472
[sobbing]

418
00:22:29,514 --> 00:22:30,557
Hey!

419
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:32,851
I hope Grandpa catches you watching.

420
00:22:34,394 --> 00:22:37,606
[somber music playing]

421
00:22:37,689 --> 00:22:40,525
Stop that. You sound like a dying pig.

422
00:22:40,609 --> 00:22:44,571
Aren't you used to Mommy
and Daddy fighting?

423
00:22:44,654 --> 00:22:47,783
If Grandpa hears you crying,
he'll serve you for dinner.

424
00:22:47,866 --> 00:22:49,159
You baby pig.

425
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:53,288
[sobbing]

426
00:22:54,414 --> 00:22:57,334
[Maan] Get inside now, kids. Get inside.

427
00:22:58,126 --> 00:23:01,129
-Teacher!
-She's here, Ms. Maan!

428
00:23:01,213 --> 00:23:02,923
Hi. Good morning!

429
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:04,883
Good morning!

430
00:23:04,966 --> 00:23:08,261
Good morning. I'm Camia Cruz.

431
00:23:08,345 --> 00:23:09,971
Oh, the one from Manila.

432
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:11,640
You teach social studies, right?

433
00:23:11,723 --> 00:23:14,601
-Yes.
-Is she your daughter, Lily?

434
00:23:14,684 --> 00:23:15,769
She's in sixth grade, right?

435
00:23:15,852 --> 00:23:19,648
-Yes, I'm Lily. Good morning.
-Hello.

436
00:23:19,731 --> 00:23:22,359
I noticed the school has a new building.

437
00:23:22,442 --> 00:23:25,529
Yes, it was the project
of Governor Ardiente.

438
00:23:25,612 --> 00:23:27,364
They'll have that building blessed soon.

439
00:23:27,447 --> 00:23:30,992
Ms. Maan here is helping the students
for the dance presentation.

440
00:23:31,618 --> 00:23:33,370
[Maan] I'm actually feeling pressured.

441
00:23:33,453 --> 00:23:35,914
Especially because
the Ardientes will be there.

442
00:23:35,997 --> 00:23:40,168
The Ardientes must be
very important people.

443
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:44,172
The Ardientes provide
for this town's needs.

444
00:23:44,256 --> 00:23:46,716
We're all so grateful to their family.

445
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:50,220
We pay for everything
the politicians do for us

446
00:23:50,303 --> 00:23:51,721
with our taxes.

447
00:23:52,305 --> 00:23:55,433
They're merely managing those funds.

448
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:58,770
It's all right to thank them
for doing their jobs properly,

449
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:02,774
but we don't owe them anything.
It's not their money.

450
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:06,153
They're using the public's taxes.

451
00:24:08,071 --> 00:24:13,535
Hey, loosen up. We can't
have you starting a rally here.

452
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:15,328
What's important

453
00:24:15,412 --> 00:24:18,290
is that our officials
aren't neglecting us, right?

454
00:24:18,373 --> 00:24:19,207
[teacher] Right.

455
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:23,044
We should get inside
before the bell rings.

456
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:25,797
Oh. Lily!

457
00:24:26,756 --> 00:24:27,799
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

458
00:24:32,596 --> 00:24:37,184
Isn't today the distribution
of your report cards?

459
00:24:37,893 --> 00:24:39,227
How are your grades?

460
00:24:39,311 --> 00:24:41,938
They're good, Grandpa.
I'm still in the top five.

461
00:24:42,814 --> 00:24:46,985
Hmm… Very good! Very good! Impressive.

462
00:24:47,068 --> 00:24:49,237
But I know you can do better, Arnaldo.

463
00:24:50,447 --> 00:24:53,700
I will expect you to be number one

464
00:24:53,783 --> 00:24:55,660
by the next grading period, okay?

465
00:24:55,744 --> 00:24:56,578
Okay, Grandpa.

466
00:24:58,538 --> 00:25:01,708
How about you, Diego? How are your grades?

467
00:25:04,377 --> 00:25:06,213
Can you hear me or not?

468
00:25:06,296 --> 00:25:10,550
Oh! Uh… Here it is, sir.

469
00:25:16,723 --> 00:25:20,518
A 75 in science…

470
00:25:21,269 --> 00:25:22,395
How come?

471
00:25:22,479 --> 00:25:26,274
Our science topics were hard.
They were about insects.

472
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:29,027
Let's just get him a new tutor.

473
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:32,364
[Emilia] You might be sleeping
in class again.

474
00:25:32,447 --> 00:25:35,909
Starting tomorrow, I'm going
to put you on a diet. Okay?

475
00:25:35,992 --> 00:25:37,452
He's always full!

476
00:25:37,535 --> 00:25:39,454
-And then--
-Arnaldo!

477
00:25:41,122 --> 00:25:42,874
He only needs one belly rub

478
00:25:42,958 --> 00:25:46,211
before he falls asleep like a pig!
It's true!

479
00:25:46,294 --> 00:25:47,921
I told you to stop!

480
00:25:48,004 --> 00:25:49,965
-Are you testing me?
-Shut up!

481
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:52,175
[tense music playing]

482
00:25:55,470 --> 00:25:58,431
You two… Get ready for tomorrow.

483
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:07,983
-[tapping]
-[foreboding music playing]

484
00:26:10,652 --> 00:26:11,903
Good morning, Grandpa.

485
00:26:12,570 --> 00:26:13,738
Good morning!

486
00:26:16,783 --> 00:26:17,826
Diego!

487
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:20,787
Diego!

488
00:26:22,163 --> 00:26:25,208
Who do you think you're kidding?

489
00:26:25,292 --> 00:26:26,293
[shouts] One!

490
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:33,341
Grandpa, why are we here?

491
00:26:34,134 --> 00:26:35,677
You know what this is, right?

492
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:37,304
Our properties?

493
00:26:37,387 --> 00:26:39,556
That's Poblacion Ardiente.

494
00:26:39,639 --> 00:26:40,974
That's right!

495
00:26:41,808 --> 00:26:45,812
Did you know that every corner
of Poblacion Ardiente

496
00:26:45,895 --> 00:26:49,232
is etched in my mind? But you…

497
00:26:49,316 --> 00:26:52,736
You have to study this
until you can see it

498
00:26:52,819 --> 00:26:55,155
even with your eyes closed.

499
00:26:55,238 --> 00:27:00,076
Until you can control every piece of it
from wherever you are.

500
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:04,247
That is the mark of a true leader.

501
00:27:05,206 --> 00:27:08,543
People are always in need of a leader.

502
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:11,755
Just like those ants…

503
00:27:14,007 --> 00:27:16,343
That is the house of the warrior ants.

504
00:27:16,968 --> 00:27:20,638
They're big, red, and feisty.

505
00:27:20,722 --> 00:27:22,390
[Arnaldo] Ouch! Ouch!

506
00:27:22,932 --> 00:27:25,852
[Julio] They need to be strong and feisty

507
00:27:25,935 --> 00:27:28,438
because they protect the queen.

508
00:27:29,064 --> 00:27:33,151
The queen is the biggest,
and she is the one who sustains them all.

509
00:27:33,943 --> 00:27:38,365
That's how we, Ardientes,
are to the people of this town,

510
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:42,285
because we are the strong ones.

511
00:27:43,578 --> 00:27:48,208
Now, look at the other hill.
What do you see? Diego?

512
00:27:49,667 --> 00:27:55,548
I see black ants crawling
and carrying food.

513
00:27:55,632 --> 00:27:59,135
Food for the soldier ants,

514
00:27:59,219 --> 00:28:01,221
the queen,

515
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:06,559
and everyone stronger than them.

516
00:28:07,143 --> 00:28:08,686
They're like the people
of Ardiente, Grandpa?

517
00:28:09,270 --> 00:28:10,397
[chuckles]

518
00:28:11,231 --> 00:28:17,195
That's right! They were born to serve us.

519
00:28:17,278 --> 00:28:18,696
That's their role.

520
00:28:20,448 --> 00:28:25,787
I let these ants live for you, Diego.

521
00:28:26,454 --> 00:28:27,789
For me?

522
00:28:27,872 --> 00:28:30,583
Uh… Thank you?

523
00:28:33,837 --> 00:28:36,131
Not only does he have a weak mind,

524
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:39,342
but a weak body as well.

525
00:28:39,426 --> 00:28:41,720
Did you think you could get away with it?

526
00:28:42,303 --> 00:28:44,973
-With what, Grandpa?
-Every freaking year…

527
00:28:45,056 --> 00:28:47,559
you fail one subject in school!

528
00:28:47,642 --> 00:28:49,769
I don't know
what's in that brain of yours!

529
00:28:49,853 --> 00:28:50,770
Maybe it's filled with fat too!

530
00:28:50,854 --> 00:28:51,938
[crying]

531
00:28:52,021 --> 00:28:54,482
You're a disgrace to the family!

532
00:28:54,566 --> 00:28:56,109
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

533
00:28:56,192 --> 00:28:58,611
I'll study harder next time.

534
00:28:58,695 --> 00:29:00,071
-I promise.
-[Julio] You better!

535
00:29:00,155 --> 00:29:03,575
Stand over there, and don't move until
I tell you to. Understood?!

536
00:29:04,242 --> 00:29:05,326
Stand over there!

537
00:29:06,035 --> 00:29:10,165
Grandpa! Grandpa! Ouch!

538
00:29:10,665 --> 00:29:12,625
-[sobbing]
-[Julio] Take it like a man!

539
00:29:12,709 --> 00:29:15,920
Don't scratch the ants away.
Stand straight!

540
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:18,339
-[Diego] Please stop. It hurts!
-[Julio] Endure the pain!

541
00:29:19,966 --> 00:29:23,303
-You have to become a real Ardiente!
-[Diego] Grandpa, please. It really hurts.

542
00:29:23,386 --> 00:29:25,722
[sobbing] It really hurts.

543
00:29:26,556 --> 00:29:28,683
[Diego] Grandpa, make it stop.

544
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:35,023
[serene music playing]

545
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:45,033
[Camia] Here. Have some snacks.

546
00:29:45,116 --> 00:29:47,702
Wow! Those look yummy!

547
00:29:51,372 --> 00:29:53,958
[hammering]

548
00:29:55,627 --> 00:29:57,462
[serene music playing]

549
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:18,942
[Diego sobbing]

550
00:30:21,486 --> 00:30:23,446
[somber music playing]

551
00:30:23,530 --> 00:30:25,281
[Julio] <i>Not only are your mind</i>
<i>and body weak,</i>

552
00:30:25,365 --> 00:30:29,369
<i>you can't follow orders, either!</i>
<i>You're a disgrace to the family!</i>

553
00:30:30,203 --> 00:30:33,206
[Diego] <i>Grandpa's right. Everyone's right.</i>

554
00:30:33,289 --> 00:30:35,083
<i>I have to be brave.</i>

555
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:36,835
[sniffles]

556
00:30:36,918 --> 00:30:39,087
<i>I have to endure the pain.</i>

557
00:30:40,672 --> 00:30:42,507
<i>No one in the Ardiente family is weak.</i>

558
00:30:44,843 --> 00:30:47,178
[foreboding music playing]

559
00:30:47,262 --> 00:30:48,763
[Lily chuckles]

560
00:30:52,392 --> 00:30:53,351
Oh.

561
00:30:53,434 --> 00:30:56,145
[beautiful, serene music playing]

562
00:30:57,063 --> 00:31:01,234
Wow! This place is beautiful! [chuckles]

563
00:31:03,194 --> 00:31:05,488
[crying]

564
00:31:08,825 --> 00:31:13,454
[suspenseful music playing]

565
00:31:13,538 --> 00:31:15,290
[breathing heavily]

566
00:31:16,749 --> 00:31:18,084
Hey, don't jump!

567
00:31:18,835 --> 00:31:21,588
-[Diego screaming]
-Oh, no!

568
00:31:21,671 --> 00:31:25,049
Help! Help me!

569
00:31:26,509 --> 00:31:28,511
[sobbing]

570
00:31:28,595 --> 00:31:30,638
-[Lily] Hey!
-Help me!

571
00:31:30,722 --> 00:31:31,931
Grab my hand! Hurry!

572
00:31:33,266 --> 00:31:34,642
-Help me.
-Slowly!

573
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:36,978
-That's it! Slowly!
-[sobbing continues]

574
00:31:37,061 --> 00:31:39,814
Get up! Be careful!

575
00:31:40,690 --> 00:31:42,108
[Lily] Come on. [panting]

576
00:31:43,818 --> 00:31:44,819
Watch your step.

577
00:31:46,404 --> 00:31:49,407
-Why did you jump?
-I didn't jump!

578
00:31:49,490 --> 00:31:52,327
I saw you jump! Good thing I saw you!

579
00:31:52,410 --> 00:31:54,120
[Diego] What are you talking about?

580
00:31:54,203 --> 00:31:58,499
-[Lily] Hey, watch your step!
-[Diego] You're the reason I almost fell.

581
00:31:59,125 --> 00:32:00,168
What?

582
00:32:01,169 --> 00:32:03,671
If it weren't for me,
you would've fallen off the cliff.

583
00:32:03,755 --> 00:32:06,132
So, you're a hero? Who are you?
Wonder Woman?

584
00:32:06,215 --> 00:32:09,344
[exhales sharply] No. My name is Lily.

585
00:32:09,427 --> 00:32:12,972
But it's a good thing
I was here to save you.

586
00:32:13,765 --> 00:32:16,142
Why? Because I'm weak?

587
00:32:20,229 --> 00:32:23,066
I know I'm weak.

588
00:32:23,691 --> 00:32:26,819
[sniffles] That's all
my grandfather ever tells me.

589
00:32:26,903 --> 00:32:28,988
I get it. I'm weak.

590
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:35,328
-[somber music playing]
-[sobbing]

591
00:32:37,747 --> 00:32:40,291
Hey, that's not what I meant.

592
00:32:40,375 --> 00:32:41,918
[sobbing continues]

593
00:32:42,001 --> 00:32:42,961
I'm sorry.

594
00:32:45,129 --> 00:32:47,215
-You're wounded.
-[sniffles]

595
00:32:47,298 --> 00:32:48,383
Hold on.

596
00:32:54,389 --> 00:32:56,182
[beautiful, serene music playing]

597
00:33:11,072 --> 00:33:12,365
Why do you have all those rashes?

598
00:33:12,448 --> 00:33:14,158
What happened to you?

599
00:33:19,122 --> 00:33:20,289
What's your name?

600
00:33:21,332 --> 00:33:23,001
I'm nobody. I have to go.

601
00:33:23,084 --> 00:33:26,087
Wait! You look familiar.

602
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:28,881
Are you Governor Ardiente's grandson?

603
00:33:29,716 --> 00:33:31,342
What are you doing here?

604
00:33:31,426 --> 00:33:33,219
I'm here to study.

605
00:33:33,302 --> 00:33:35,888
-[Camia] Lily?
-[Dante] Lily!

606
00:33:37,807 --> 00:33:38,975
Those are my parents.

607
00:33:39,058 --> 00:33:41,644
Do you want to visit our house?

608
00:33:41,728 --> 00:33:44,772
No, thanks. My family
might be looking for me.

609
00:33:44,856 --> 00:33:47,567
Too bad. My mom prepared some snacks.

610
00:33:47,650 --> 00:33:50,778
We have banana fritters. Come on.

611
00:33:53,656 --> 00:33:56,868
Uh… Thanks. But maybe another day.

612
00:33:58,578 --> 00:34:02,290
All right. Don't go near
the cliff again, okay?

613
00:34:02,373 --> 00:34:03,374
Okay.

614
00:34:06,377 --> 00:34:09,130
-Take care.
-Thanks.

615
00:34:14,510 --> 00:34:20,475
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

616
00:34:26,189 --> 00:34:28,649
Mom. [chuckles]

617
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:29,942
[Camia] Lily.

618
00:34:30,651 --> 00:34:32,028
Wow!

619
00:34:32,111 --> 00:34:36,365
I didn't know this was near our house.
What a beautiful garden!

620
00:34:36,449 --> 00:34:38,618
This isn't a garden, Dad. It's a paradise!

621
00:34:38,701 --> 00:34:41,954
[all chuckling]

622
00:34:45,666 --> 00:34:51,798
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

623
00:34:58,387 --> 00:35:00,223
[groans softly]

624
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:04,852
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

625
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:13,444
ARDIENTE TOWN

626
00:35:14,862 --> 00:35:17,448
[man] This will be your table, Atty. Cruz.

627
00:35:17,532 --> 00:35:18,699
[Dante] Call me Dante.

628
00:35:18,783 --> 00:35:22,120
[man] Your degree would be a waste
without the title, Attorney.

629
00:35:22,203 --> 00:35:24,080
I'm Atty. Pablo.

630
00:35:24,163 --> 00:35:25,039
Hello.

631
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:27,083
-These are Atty. Villacruz…
-Hi, there.

632
00:35:27,166 --> 00:35:30,378
Atty. Galliego, and Atty. Sta. Maria.

633
00:35:30,461 --> 00:35:31,796
Attorney.

634
00:35:31,879 --> 00:35:33,089
[Atty. Villacruz] Are you from Manila?

635
00:35:33,172 --> 00:35:35,883
Oh, I'm sure you'll find
this place different.

636
00:35:35,967 --> 00:35:37,385
How come?

637
00:35:37,468 --> 00:35:38,886
Legal battles are rare here.

638
00:35:38,970 --> 00:35:41,848
For the past 15 years,
there's practically been no crime!

639
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:44,976
So I've read on the town's website.

640
00:35:45,059 --> 00:35:46,227
How did that happen?

641
00:35:46,310 --> 00:35:50,690
I'm sorry, but it's hard to
believe there's no crime here.

642
00:35:52,733 --> 00:35:54,610
You really shouldn't believe it.

643
00:35:55,278 --> 00:35:57,113
That's Arthur, our clerk.

644
00:35:57,196 --> 00:36:00,449
He's the key to the zero crime rate.

645
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:03,327
That's not true! This place is pure evil.

646
00:36:03,411 --> 00:36:05,580
Someday, this town will cease to exist.

647
00:36:06,622 --> 00:36:08,124
[Atty. Villacruz] Don't
pay attention to him.

648
00:36:08,207 --> 00:36:09,458
His screws are a little loose.

649
00:36:09,542 --> 00:36:11,419
[laughing]

650
00:36:12,587 --> 00:36:14,505
[foreboding music playing]

651
00:36:17,425 --> 00:36:19,343
[Dante] That's what
he was saying in the office.

652
00:36:19,427 --> 00:36:21,053
Do you think it's true?

653
00:36:21,137 --> 00:36:25,808
Come on, hon. Your co-workers did say
Arthur has a mental condition.

654
00:36:26,601 --> 00:36:28,519
Do you believe

655
00:36:28,603 --> 00:36:31,772
what Mr. Arthur said
about this town disappearing?

656
00:36:32,356 --> 00:36:36,194
Only God knows the future, Lily.

657
00:36:36,777 --> 00:36:40,114
If we continue to be kindhearted,
then we have nothing to fear.

658
00:36:40,698 --> 00:36:41,699
That's true.

659
00:36:41,782 --> 00:36:44,869
There you have it,
but you're still suspicious.

660
00:36:44,952 --> 00:36:47,413
Oh, hon, stop it.

661
00:36:47,496 --> 00:36:49,707
Don't meddle in other people's lives.

662
00:36:49,790 --> 00:36:52,251
[soft music playing]

663
00:36:57,089 --> 00:36:58,716
-Lily.
-Lily, are you done eating?

664
00:36:59,300 --> 00:37:00,676
[Lily] Yes, Dad. How about you?

665
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:01,802
[Dante] I'm done too.

666
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:03,679
[Lily] You still have so much
on your plate.

667
00:37:04,263 --> 00:37:06,098
I mean, I'm done with this.

668
00:37:08,309 --> 00:37:11,604
Wow! [chuckles] <i>365 Days?</i>

669
00:37:11,687 --> 00:37:14,273
For an entire year full of love.

670
00:37:14,357 --> 00:37:16,067
[Camia] Yeah, right.

671
00:37:16,150 --> 00:37:19,737
More like 365 days
of your father-daughter banter!

672
00:37:19,820 --> 00:37:21,864
-[Lily chuckles] Come on, Mom!
-[Camia] I'm just saying.

673
00:37:21,948 --> 00:37:23,866
-[Camia and Lily laughing]
-[playful music playing]

674
00:37:23,950 --> 00:37:26,827
Yuck! Yuck! Yuck!

675
00:37:29,038 --> 00:37:29,872
Diego?

676
00:37:30,706 --> 00:37:31,874
I'm sorry.

677
00:37:33,709 --> 00:37:34,627
[Lily] Diego, wait!

678
00:37:35,836 --> 00:37:37,088
Why are you always in a rush?

679
00:37:37,171 --> 00:37:38,422
I was on my way home.

680
00:37:38,506 --> 00:37:40,549
Were you supposed to do
your homework here?

681
00:37:42,176 --> 00:37:45,471
You still can. Come here!

682
00:37:45,554 --> 00:37:46,973
-[soft piano music playing]
-Come on!

683
00:37:49,308 --> 00:37:52,061
Mom, Dad, this is Diego.

684
00:37:52,144 --> 00:37:54,605
-Good afternoon.
-[Dante] Good afternoon.

685
00:37:56,565 --> 00:37:58,526
-Oh, never mind.
-[Camia chuckles]

686
00:37:58,609 --> 00:38:01,612
Oh, Diego, come over here.
I'll clean that up.

687
00:38:03,864 --> 00:38:06,284
[soft piano music playing]

688
00:38:06,367 --> 00:38:07,493
[Camia] There.

689
00:38:13,457 --> 00:38:15,251
-What happened?
-I was bit.

690
00:38:17,295 --> 00:38:18,546
I was bitten by ants.

691
00:38:19,297 --> 00:38:21,090
[gloomy music playing]

692
00:38:22,591 --> 00:38:24,885
-Diego, come sit.
-Come.

693
00:38:26,679 --> 00:38:28,723
-Eat up, Diego.
-Join us.

694
00:38:28,806 --> 00:38:30,182
This one's good.

695
00:38:30,266 --> 00:38:32,268
-Thank you.
-Diego, what grade are you in?

696
00:38:32,351 --> 00:38:33,477
Fourth grade, sir.

697
00:38:34,729 --> 00:38:36,314
You come all the way here to study?

698
00:38:36,397 --> 00:38:40,276
Yes. It's quiet here. I can focus more.

699
00:38:40,359 --> 00:38:43,237
Very good! He's serious about studying!

700
00:38:43,321 --> 00:38:47,283
I need to be. They're getting mad at me.

701
00:38:47,366 --> 00:38:50,286
-[soft piano music playing]
-[Lily sighs]

702
00:38:50,369 --> 00:38:55,249
Hey, don't be sad.
We can help you if you want.

703
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:56,792
[Lily] My mom's a teacher.

704
00:38:56,876 --> 00:39:00,046
You'll get better grades
if you let her help you.

705
00:39:00,129 --> 00:39:01,672
For how much?

706
00:39:01,756 --> 00:39:03,966
-I'll tell Mommy and Daddy.
-[chuckles]

707
00:39:04,050 --> 00:39:05,801
Oh, it's for free.

708
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:10,598
Just behave well during our classes.

709
00:39:10,681 --> 00:39:11,599
Thank you.

710
00:39:12,183 --> 00:39:13,684
-You should eat first.
-Go on.

711
00:39:13,768 --> 00:39:15,853
-[Lily] Try that.
-[Camia] I tried this a while ago.

712
00:39:15,936 --> 00:39:19,482
-[both chuckle]
-I finished ahead of you.

713
00:39:19,565 --> 00:39:21,817
[soft music playing]

714
00:39:21,901 --> 00:39:23,069
[Lily] That's the end of the story.

715
00:39:23,152 --> 00:39:25,321
[Camia] Well, since story time is over,
go have some banana fritters.

716
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:27,907
-Go get some.
-Here, drink this.

717
00:39:27,990 --> 00:39:30,326
-[Lily] It's delicious.
-[Loring] There.

718
00:39:30,409 --> 00:39:31,952
[Camia] Eat up. Don't be shy.

719
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:33,537
Are you done? Or you dropped it?

720
00:39:33,621 --> 00:39:36,082
[Camia] Stay here for a while.
Yummy, right?

721
00:39:38,292 --> 00:39:39,418
Get another one.

722
00:39:39,502 --> 00:39:40,878
No, thanks. I'm full.

723
00:39:40,961 --> 00:39:44,215
[clicks tongue] Diego, eat some more.
There's more inside.

724
00:39:44,965 --> 00:39:47,385
Come on, Diego. Get some.

725
00:39:48,761 --> 00:39:50,679
[rooster crowing in distance]

726
00:39:53,516 --> 00:39:57,061
You're full, huh? You're so cute!

727
00:39:57,144 --> 00:39:58,521
[laughs]

728
00:40:07,196 --> 00:40:09,407
Diego, do you need help?

729
00:40:10,991 --> 00:40:12,410
Here.

730
00:40:12,493 --> 00:40:13,744
-Are you done?
-Yeah.

731
00:40:13,828 --> 00:40:14,912
That was fast.

732
00:40:15,496 --> 00:40:18,582
I hope my grades get better.

733
00:40:19,166 --> 00:40:21,043
-You got it all right.
-Really?

734
00:40:21,127 --> 00:40:23,838
You got a perfect score! Good job!

735
00:40:24,964 --> 00:40:26,132
[both chuckle]

736
00:40:26,215 --> 00:40:27,508
Thanks, Lily.

737
00:40:27,591 --> 00:40:28,926
No problem.

738
00:40:29,844 --> 00:40:32,346
I wish Grandpa would be proud of me.

739
00:40:33,055 --> 00:40:34,348
And Mom too.

740
00:40:34,432 --> 00:40:37,143
And I wish I weren't hungry all the time,

741
00:40:37,226 --> 00:40:39,728
so I won't be fat anymore.

742
00:40:39,812 --> 00:40:42,982
I wish… they'll love me.

743
00:40:44,775 --> 00:40:45,609
Diego…

744
00:40:46,485 --> 00:40:48,195
They're your family, and they love you.

745
00:40:48,279 --> 00:40:50,114
Maybe it just isn't obvious.

746
00:40:50,197 --> 00:40:52,825
No. Grandpa's not like that.

747
00:40:53,409 --> 00:40:55,744
He always gets mad because I'm fat.

748
00:40:55,828 --> 00:40:59,039
I can't help that I like to eat.

749
00:41:00,416 --> 00:41:04,462
Oh, you. It's okay to eat,
but not too much. [laughs]

750
00:41:05,588 --> 00:41:06,630
Oh!

751
00:41:06,714 --> 00:41:09,675
I'll teach you how to lose
weight even if you eat a lot!

752
00:41:10,342 --> 00:41:12,303
-Really? How?
-Yes, it's pretty easy!

753
00:41:12,386 --> 00:41:13,971
Come with me! Hurry!

754
00:41:14,054 --> 00:41:16,348
Ready, get set, go!

755
00:41:17,224 --> 00:41:19,185
-[lively music playing]
-Go, Diego! Bend over!

756
00:41:19,268 --> 00:41:21,896
You can do it, come on! Keep running!

757
00:41:21,979 --> 00:41:23,355
-Oh, my!
-[Diego grunts]

758
00:41:24,064 --> 00:41:27,526
I told you to be careful.
Can you still do it?

759
00:41:27,610 --> 00:41:28,611
-I can.
-All right!

760
00:41:28,694 --> 00:41:30,446
-Yeah.
-You did it! You got it all!

761
00:41:30,529 --> 00:41:31,822
-Yay!
-Yay!

762
00:41:31,906 --> 00:41:35,701
Great job, Diego!
You did it! You ran that far!

763
00:41:37,286 --> 00:41:39,079
[lively music playing]

764
00:41:43,167 --> 00:41:46,462
[Lily] Just swing the rope, and then…

765
00:41:46,545 --> 00:41:49,089
Like this? Be careful.

766
00:41:50,466 --> 00:41:52,051
Skip, like this. Let's do it together.

767
00:41:52,134 --> 00:41:53,594
-Swing the rope…
-Swing the rope…

768
00:41:54,136 --> 00:41:55,763
It's easy.

769
00:41:55,846 --> 00:41:57,223
-I did it!
-[Lily] See?

770
00:41:57,306 --> 00:41:59,058
Let's skip ten times.

771
00:41:59,141 --> 00:42:02,853
[together] Seven, eight, nine, ten!

772
00:42:02,937 --> 00:42:05,147
Yay! We did it!

773
00:42:06,023 --> 00:42:07,525
-One…
-Wait, how?

774
00:42:07,608 --> 00:42:09,026
Like this.

775
00:42:09,109 --> 00:42:10,861
-Like this?
-Higher.

776
00:42:10,945 --> 00:42:14,114
Feet apart. Then, close them. One…

777
00:42:15,783 --> 00:42:17,076
-Eight, nine…
-Eight, nine…

778
00:42:17,159 --> 00:42:18,744
-Last one!
-Ten!

779
00:42:22,414 --> 00:42:24,041
-Reach for me.
-[grunts]

780
00:42:24,124 --> 00:42:28,087
You can do it! Keep going! Last one!

781
00:42:28,170 --> 00:42:32,132
Five! Let's try again.

782
00:42:32,216 --> 00:42:34,885
[lively music playing]

783
00:42:34,969 --> 00:42:39,974
Ready, set, go!
You can do it, Diego! Come on!

784
00:42:40,057 --> 00:42:43,185
Go, Diego! Keep running!

785
00:42:44,603 --> 00:42:49,316
Ten! Good job, Diego!
You finished all rounds!

786
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:53,279
I knew you could do it.
It was hard, but you made it!

787
00:42:53,362 --> 00:42:55,364
Just tell yourself you can do it.

788
00:42:58,534 --> 00:43:00,035
Good job! [chuckles]

789
00:43:00,119 --> 00:43:01,537
You can rest now.

790
00:43:01,620 --> 00:43:02,746
Lily.

791
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:06,000
Thanks for helping me out.

792
00:43:06,667 --> 00:43:07,918
[chuckles]

793
00:43:08,002 --> 00:43:09,920
No worries! I got you.

794
00:43:12,464 --> 00:43:14,925
[soft music playing]

795
00:43:16,885 --> 00:43:18,387
[Loring] Eat up, okay?

796
00:43:18,470 --> 00:43:21,432
You got a perfect score
for the first time!

797
00:43:21,515 --> 00:43:24,226
[chuckles] I'm sure
your grades will get better.

798
00:43:24,310 --> 00:43:27,479
What? What's perfect?

799
00:43:27,563 --> 00:43:30,816
My exam scores.
Teacher Camia is tutoring me.

800
00:43:30,899 --> 00:43:34,320
-Hmm.
-She's the mom of my new friend, Lily.

801
00:43:37,531 --> 00:43:38,699
[Lily] Mom.

802
00:43:38,782 --> 00:43:41,160
-Lily.
-[Lily] I asked them to come.

803
00:43:41,243 --> 00:43:43,621
-[Camia] Wow! Have a seat.
-[Lily] Sit there.

804
00:43:44,204 --> 00:43:45,289
You can play with these.

805
00:43:45,372 --> 00:43:47,291
-Do you want the bigger one?
-[Camia] These?

806
00:43:47,374 --> 00:43:48,709
[Lily] Mom, can they play for a while?

807
00:43:48,792 --> 00:43:50,002
-[Camia] Sure, go ahead.
-[Diego] Good day!

808
00:43:50,085 --> 00:43:51,086
-[Lily] Hey, Diego!
-[Loring] Good morning!

809
00:43:51,170 --> 00:43:52,880
-[Camia] Diego.
-[Lily] Good morning.

810
00:43:52,963 --> 00:43:54,214
[Loring] Good day.

811
00:43:54,298 --> 00:43:57,968
[foreboding music playing]

812
00:44:34,922 --> 00:44:38,217
<i>-You're more beautiful up close.</i>
<i>-Don't touch me!</i>

813
00:44:38,300 --> 00:44:40,386
<i>Did your wife tell you</i>
<i>about what happened yesterday at school?</i>

814
00:44:40,469 --> 00:44:41,679
<i>I didn't want any trouble.</i>

815
00:44:42,388 --> 00:44:44,014
<i>You're just going to keep quiet</i>
<i>after what he did?</i>

816
00:44:44,098 --> 00:44:45,766
[Julio]<i> It's all over the news.</i>

817
00:44:45,849 --> 00:44:49,269
<i>Your devoted husband</i>
<i>didn't use his brain again.</i>

818
00:44:49,353 --> 00:44:51,271
<i>Fix this, Emilia.</i>

819
00:44:51,355 --> 00:44:53,023
<i>Our political enemies</i>
<i>might get wind of this.</i>

820
00:44:53,107 --> 00:44:55,901
[man] <i>Atty. Cruz, the mayor's</i>
<i>inviting you to her office.</i>

821
00:44:55,984 --> 00:44:57,403
<i>I'm not afraid of you!</i>

822
00:44:57,486 --> 00:44:58,862
<i>You won't win.</i>

823
00:45:00,406 --> 00:45:01,698
-[groans]
-[tires screeching]

824
00:45:01,782 --> 00:45:02,991
<i>Dante!</i>

825
00:45:03,075 --> 00:45:05,285
-[tires screeching]
-[loud crash]

826
00:45:05,369 --> 00:45:07,037
<i>Good job!</i>

827
00:45:07,121 --> 00:45:09,998
[theme music playing]
